@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam PackageBorderColor #9ca3af
skinparam ArtifactBorderColor #6b7280

title A requirement is stated against a tool; a value lives on a page. SpecialtyFilter serves two pages and holds different values on each.

package "The declaration — the registry entry\n(one record, generated from source at build)" {
  component "tool: SpecialtyFilter\n(its entry in the registry)" as Tool #dcfce7

  artifact "complaint — input field, Required" as PComplaint
  artifact "offeredSpecialties — input field, Optional" as POffered
  artifact "selectedSpecialtyCodes — input field, Optional" as PSelected

  component "page: individualProvider\nProviderSearch, SpecialtyFilter,\nProviderDetail, ProviderSelection" as PageIP #f3f4f6
  component "page: NUCC\nSpecialtyFilter" as PageNUCC #f3f4f6
}

PComplaint -down-> Tool : input field of
POffered -down-> Tool : input field of
PSelected -down-> Tool : input field of

Tool -down-> PageIP : composed into
Tool -down-> PageNUCC : composed into

note right of Tool
  Stated once, against the tool, and never against a page.
  The required flags are the tool's prerequisites: the
  UniversalNavigator's completeness test reads the passed
  document against them before it dispatches.
  A page carries several tools — a search, a chooser, a
  detail, a selection — each with its own answer, and the
  search runs before any record is opened. Requiring the
  detail's parameter of the page would stop the search that
  comes first.
end note

database "The session\nuserParameters.pages" as Session

package "values, one set per page" {
  artifact "pages.individualProvider\n  complaint\n  selectedSpecialtyCodes\n  state / city / county / zip\n  providerName, providerSex,\n  soleProprietor, insurance\n  openNpi" as VIP #fef3c7
  artifact "pages.NUCC\n  complaint\n  offeredSpecialties\n  selectedSpecialtyCodes" as VNUCC #fef3c7
}

Session -down-> VIP
Session -down-> VNUCC

PageIP ..> VIP : its scope
PageNUCC ..> VNUCC : its scope

component "/provider/find\nclient_sessioned route" as RIP
component "/specialty/find\nclient_sessioned route" as RNUCC

RIP -up-> VIP : writes complaint and\nselectedSpecialtyCodes here
RNUCC -up-> VNUCC : writes complaint, offeredSpecialties\nand selectedSpecialtyCodes here

component "UniversalNavigator\ncodes_in_force() — parameters + state" as Reader

Reader -up-> VIP : reads selectedSpecialtyCodes first
Reader -up-> VNUCC : falls back to offeredSpecialties

note bottom of Reader
  The navigator tracks all parameters and their state; a
  conflict is an exception. The same three names on two
  pages hold two different answers. Nothing chosen on the
  care-giver page means the person has not narrowed, so the
  whole set the NUCC panel offered still applies. Neither
  page could express that if a value had one home.
end note

note bottom of VIP
  openNpi is held here and on the facility page, and the
  record declares no parameter of that name. openNctId, the
  trial equivalent, is declared. Drawn as the code does it.
end note

note bottom of RNUCC
  This page finds nobody. It is where a person waits while
  their geography is not yet usable, so what it produces is
  the panel and the codes it is ticked with, and nothing
  else. A turn naming no complaint does not withdraw the one
  already in force — repainting the panel empty would take
  the person's choices away.
end note

@enduml
